::  name       comlink address width gate
::  shape      bytes - int (@u32) -> lawful - int (@u32)
::  invariant  answers 1 while an address width stays within sixteen bytes; answers 0 past the wall
::  example    4 -> 1 · 16 -> 1 · 20 -> 0
::  readers    Comlink · Glow Tend R1 · Ashvini
::  nib        equinox-e222-comlink-addr-width-v0
::
::  Ashvini R1 · width face beside the pier policy pedestal — STOA331 grammar.
::  The seated shape names ipv4_addr_len=4 and ipv6_addr_len=16; this face makes
::  that pair runnable. Both lawful widths pass; twenty speaks 0. Sibling
::  records, never a union; the wall decides, the wire carries nothing new.
|=  sample=@u32
?:  (gth sample 16)  0  1
